    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What files does this skill inspect?",
        "answer": "It focuses on package manifests and configuration files such as package.json, pyproject.toml, go.mod, Cargo.toml, pubspec.yaml, and CMakeLists.txt."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does it install dependencies?",
        "answer": "No. The skill is designed to read manifests and classify dependency names without installing packages."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it detect test frameworks?",
        "answer": "Yes. It maps known test packages such as Vitest, Jest, pytest, Playwright, GTest, and Flutter Test when they appear in supported manifests."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does it work with monorepos?",
        "answer": "Yes. It can scan multiple manifests and report which paths support each detected stack signal."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it confirm that a library is actively used?",
        "answer": "Not by itself. It can identify manifest evidence, but imports and configuration files should be checked for usage confirmation."
